Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Sindhu-Sarasvati Valley", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:35:46Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Improve", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:36:00Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Arre bas common name bol do", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:36:02Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "or Indus Valley Civilization, a name that I think is a misnomer", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": true, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:36:13Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "I agree but wohi usual name hai", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:36:28Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "The actual name should be Indus-Ghagghar-Hakra ‎", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:36:56Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "It was technically also a twin river system like Mesopotamia", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:37:34Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "big difference is that the two didn’t meet before reaching the sea, like the Euphrates and the Tigris", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:37:47Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "they came very close upstream in the Punjab", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:37:59Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Oh I didn't know that. Very interesting", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:38:27Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "In the sense that I didn't know that the Tigris and the Euphrates met", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:39:10Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "yeah they meet just before heading to the sea, like the Ganga and Brahmaputra meet just before the delta", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:39:21Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Oh okay. Got it", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:39:44Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Speaking of which, the Indo-Gangetic plains should actually be called the Indo-Gangetic-Brahmaputra plains", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:40:30Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Idk why but it always pisses me off that they're not called so, coz the Brahmaputra is an integral part of the riverine and plains systems there ‎", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:42:55Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Brahmaputra valley wasn’t controlled by the empires in the Gangetic plain for most of history, that’s probably why historians don’t treat it as one system ‎", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:43:59Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Yes but the nomenclature is recent, during which the Brahmaputra region was indeed under British control. Also, once you look at the overall plains region, it's hard to ignore the Brahmaputra as another central river there", "role": "confirmation", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:44:16Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "whereas most major empires controlled both Ganga and Sindhu valleys", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:44:54Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Yes that is true. But they did extent into the borders of Assam, and definition controlled most of Bengal. And those regions do have the Brahmaputra ‎", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:44:55Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "i agree with you about the geography. i am just speculating about reasons why historians don’t treat it as one contiguous region", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:45:13Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Yes I think it's just one those factual inaccuracies", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:46:03Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Like how historians ignore the deep cultural links between the Indian subcontinent and Xinjiang, Yunnan, and southern Central Asia while focusing on Tibet, SE Asia, and Iran wrt the periphery of the Indian subcontinent ‎", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-16T03:46:49Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Also, unrelated pt., but \"Mesopotamia\" has to be one of the most accurate regional names lol ‎", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]